 4 0\n0 4 0 4 0 4 0 4 0 4 0 4 0 4 0 4\n4 0 4 0 4 0 4 0 4 0 4 0 4 0 4 0\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1\n1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4\n4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1 4 1\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2\n2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4\n4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2 4 2\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n\nNew instance. Task id: task-abe708e5\nTest input (10x10):\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n1 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\n4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4\nWrong attempts used: 0/8. Demo requests used: 0/8.\nReply with exactly one action JSON on the last line.","reply":"","steps":[],"action":{"type":"invalid"}},{"step":45,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1793263406.91,"t1":1793264351.66,"alias":"task-abe708e5","message":"I could not find a valid action in your reply (empty reply). Reply with your program in one ```python block and {\"action\": \"submit\"} on the last line, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"","steps":[],"action":{"type":"invalid"}},{"step":45,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1793264351.663,"t1":1793265051.653,"alias":"task-abe708e5","message":"I could not find a valid action in your reply (empty reply). Reply with your program in one ```python block and {\"action\": \"submit\"} on the last line, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"To solve this task, I analyzed the 6 demonstration pairs provided. The transformation rule distinguishes between \"Interior\" and \"Boundary\" special cells based on their column index `c`. If `c` is 0 or `W-1` (column boundary), the pattern propagates to rows `r-1`, `r`, `r+1` and fills these rows with a checkerboard pattern of the special value `v` and background `bg`. Specifically, if the row index `ri` has a distance `d = |ri - r|` such that `d` is even, the pattern `v` is placed at all columns `k` having the same parity as `c`. If `d` is odd, `v` is placed at columns with the opposite parity. If `c` is an interior cell (not boundary), the pattern propagates to all rows, placing `v` at `c` for even `d` and at `c-1, c+1` for odd `d`.\n\nThe test input has background 4 and a special cell `1` at `(2, 0)`. Since `c=0`, it is a boundary case. The propagation will span rows 1, 2, and 3.\n- Row 1 (distance 1): Odd distance. Parity opposite to `c` (0 is even, so opposite is odd). Columns `1, 3, 5, 7, 9` get `1`.\n- Row 2 (distance 0): Even distance. Parity same as `c` (even). Columns `0, 2, 4, 6, 8` get `1`.\n- Row 3 (distance 1): Odd distance. Columns `1, 3, 5, 7, 9` get `1$.\n- All other rows are background `4`.\n\n```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    # Identify background (most frequent)\n    from collections import Counter\n    bg = Counter(sum(grid, []))\n    if grid:\n        bg = max(grid[0], key=lambda x: sum(row.count(x) for row in grid))\n    else: \n        return grid\n\n    H = len(grid)\n    W = len(grid[0]) if H > 0 else 0\n    \n    # Initialize output with background\n    out = [[bg for _ in range(W)] for _ in range(H)]\n    \n    # Process special cells\n    for r in range(H):\n        for c in range(W):\n            if grid[r][c] == bg:\n                continue\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            \n            # Determine boundary or interior\n            is_boundary = (c == 0 or c == W - 1)\n            \n            if is_boundary:\n                # Boundary Case: 3-row span, checkerboard fill\n                for dr in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                    ri = r + dr\n                    if 0 <= ri < H:\n                        d = abs(ri - r)\n                        # Even distance: same parity as c\n                        # Odd distance: different parity\n                        target_parity = (c % 2) if (d % 2 == 0) else (1 - c % 2)\n                        for k in range(W):\n                            if k % 2 == target_parity:\n                                out[ri][k] = v\n            else:\n                # Interior Case: Full height, sparse\n                for i in range(H):\n                    d = abs(i - r)\n                    if d % 2 == 0:\n                        out[i][c] = v\n                    else:\n                        if c - 1 >= 0:\n                            out[i][c-1] = v\n                        if c + 1 < W:\n                            out[i][c+1] = v\n    return out\n```\n\n{\"action\": \"submit\", \"grid\": [[4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4], [4, 1, 4, 1, 4, 1, 4, 1, 4, 1], [1, 4, 1, 4, 1, 4, 1, 4, 1, 4], [4, 1, 4, 1, 4, 1, 4, 1, 4, 1], [4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4], [4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4], [4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4], [4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4], [4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4], [4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4]]}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","grid":[[4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4],[4,1,4,1,4,1,4,1,4,1],[1,4,1,4,1,4,1,4,1,4],[4,1,4,1,4,1,4,1,4,1],[4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4],[4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4],[4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4],[4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4],[4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4],[4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4]],"correct":true}}]}